        "Action Definition": "Interpretability techniques, particularly concept learning [77], can be used to test whether a model is learning erroneous features or relying on irrelevant features in its predictions. This can help identify and mitigate potential risks associated with incorrect or non-informative features influencing the model’s outputs.",
